WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.040
Track real leads and stop budgets leaking.

2
00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:07.780
This is the video for module 2 of Paid Advertising with Google Ads.

3
00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:15.130
Google's bidding tools push towards whatever you tell them is a conversion, meaning a lead or a sale.

4
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:27.540
If tracking counts page views as leads, the system will happily buy more page views. So your first job is not writing ads. It is proving that the count matches reality.

5
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:34.420
Then a short weekly routine and good notes keep the client's money working for real buyers.

6
00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:46.810
Step one. The client creates the account with their own business Google account and adds their own payment method. The account and its history belong to the business, not to you.

7
00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:57.100
Step two. When sign-up pushes a quick Smart campaign, switch to Expert mode. That gives you full control of keywords, bidding and reports.

8
00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.710
Step three. Choose the country, time zone and currency carefully. Google does not let you change the currency later.

9
00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.590
Step four. Turn on 2-Step Verification for every account with access.

10
00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:20.840
And never ask for a password. Create your own free manager account and ask the client to invite you. Standard access is usually enough.

11
00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:30.790
Ifeoma runs a lesson centre in Abuja. In March, Google Ads reported 40 leads. Her own enquiry book showed only 22.

12
00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:35.520
That is 55%. Nearly half the reported leads were not real.

13
00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:44.600
The cause was one setting. The form conversion counted Every, so the thank-you page fired again whenever parents refreshed it.

14
00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:56.360
She spent 160,000 naira. The report said each lead cost 4,000 naira. The true figure was about 7,273 naira.

15
00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:02.470
She changed Count to One. Next month Google showed 25 and her book showed 23.

16
00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:18.640
Now structure. Tunde, our Ibadan solar installer, builds one Search campaign with three ad groups: solar installation, inverter installation, and repairs. Each has one clear theme, so each ad speaks to one need.

17
00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:27.990
A new account with a modest budget starts with exact and phrase match. Broad match comes later, once tracking shows steady leads.

18
00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:37.840
Before launch, he adds negative keywords like jobs, vacancy, training and diy, so job seekers do not eat his budget.

19
00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:44.210
He sets the location option to Presence, so he does not pay for searchers in other states.

20
00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:56.060
And he starts with Maximize clicks, with a maximum CPC limit of 500 naira, then switches to Maximize conversions once tracking shows steady leads.

21
00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:02.940
Every week, open the search terms report. It shows the real searches that triggered your ads.

22
00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:18.630
In Tunde's first week he spent 69,300 naira. Searches for jobs, vacancy and training cost 8,400 naira with 0 leads. That is about 12.1% of his spend, so he blocks them.

23
00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:28.050
Price searches cost 6,300 naira for 1 lead. He keeps them, but gives them their own ad group and a pricing ad.

24
00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:41.490
And one search, inverter installation bodija, gave 3 leads for 2,100 naira. He adds it as an exact match keyword. Then he writes every change in his change log.

25
00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:47.320
Launch day is when most budget mistakes happen, so use this list every time.

26
00:03:47.670 --> 00:04:06.890
Conversions tested. Location and language right. Budget is the monthly figure divided by 30.4, and the client has confirmed it in writing. Negatives attached. Every page opens fast on mobile. And every claim, like a price or warranty, confirmed by the client.

27
00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:15.350
Ad spend is charged to the client's own card, inside their own account. You get access through your manager account.

28
00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:24.690
Never run client ads on your personal card, and never take ad spend into your personal bank account. It mixes your money with theirs.

29
00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:35.470
And warn clients about callers who claim to be from Google and ask for payment. Changes and billing happen inside the account, never by sending money to a person.

30
00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:44.760
To remember. The client owns the account and pays Google directly. Make real leads your primary conversions, counted as One.

31
00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:54.480
Always compare reported leads with the client's own records. Check search terms every week and add negatives. And log every change, with the reason.

32
00:04:55.730 --> 00:05:05.690
Your tasks: audit the tracking on one website with Tag Assistant, draft a three-ad-group campaign, and run a mock week of search terms with your decisions.

33
00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:07.980
Continue with the lessons below.
